---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lede="How PRC collects, uses, and protects information on this website."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p><span class="wire" data-wire="legal-review">Draft — pending final review. A complete policy will be published before PRC collects client information through this site.</span></p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you contact PRC, book a consultation, or submit an intake form, we collect the
        information you choose to provide: your name, contact details, organization, and a
        description of your records situation. This website does not require an account to browse.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do with it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to your inquiry and schedule consultations.</li>
        <li>Prepare a written scope if you engage PRC.</li>
        <li>Send follow-up communications you've requested. You can opt out at any time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
        <li>We do not ask for sensitive documents, account numbers, or ID numbers through public website forms.</li>
        <li>We do not use your information beyond the purpose you provided it for.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Client records</h2>
      <p>
        Records entrusted to PRC by clients are governed by the engagement agreement and our
        <a href="/records-handling">Records Handling Notice</a> — including secure handling,
        access controls, retention, and return or deletion at offboarding.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <span class="wire" data-wire="email-address">contact address coming soon</span></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
